336	// the defect above — every cell's own reset only ever uncovers the *same*
337	// background the next cell immediately repaints, so nothing but that
338	// background is ever exposed between two cells. styles.Selected still wraps
339	// the joined line afterward (rowLine), painting the same background again;
340	// by then it is redundant colour, not load-bearing, and it is what still
341	// pads the row out to the full content width.
